          "content": "<div style=\"background-color:#f0f8ff; padding:15px; border:1px solid #ccc; border-radius:10px;\">\n<h1 style=\"color:#2c5aa0;\">Fluorescent Coral Reefs</h1>\n\n<div style=\"float:right; margin:10px; padding:10px; background-color:#e6f3ff; border:1px solid #99c2ff; border-radius:5px;\">\n<h3>Project Info</h3>\n<b>Type:</b> Environmental Engineering<br>\n<b>Status:</b> Active Development<br>\n<b>Implements idea:</b> [[Bioluminescent Organisms]]<br>\n<b>Start Date:</b> 2025<br>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-top:20px;\">\n<h2>Project Overview</h2>\n<p>This project aims to engineer coral reefs that can fluoresce to serve as environmental monitoring systems. By leveraging the natural bioluminescent properties of certain organisms, these coral reefs can indicate changes in water quality and environmental conditions.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background-color:#fff8dc; padding:10px; margin:15px 0; border-left: 4px solid #ffd700;\">\n<h3>Key Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Real-time environmental monitoring through fluorescence patterns</li>\n<li>Genetically modified coral that maintains natural ecosystem balance</li>\n<li>Integration with IoT sensors for data collection</li>\n<li>Scalable deployment across different marine environments</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Implementation Details</h2>\n<p>The implementation involves several phases:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Research Phase:</b> Study of natural bioluminescent organisms and their genetic mechanisms</li>\n<li><b>Design Phase:</b> Development of genetic modification protocols</li>\n<li><b>Testing Phase:</b> Controlled environment testing with various coral species</li>\n<li><b>Deployment Phase:</b> Field testing in selected marine locations</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Related Pages</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[[Bioluminescent Organisms]] - The theoretical foundation</li>\n<li>[[Marine Biotechnology]] - Related field of study</li>\n</ul>\n\n[[Category:Environmental Projects]]\n[[Category:Marine Engineering]]\n</div>"
        }
